---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="On building, thinking, and the space between engineering and wisdom.">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-20">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-display font-semibold text-primary mb-12 leading-tight">
      Building at the frontier
    </h1>

    <div class="prose max-w-none space-y-8">
      <p class="text-xl font-body text-muted leading-relaxed">
        I'm Kevin Ong—an engineer, researcher, and writer working at the intersection 
        of human agency and machine intelligence. Based in San Francisco, I build systems 
        that amplify human creativity rather than replace it.
      </p>

      <p class="font-body text-muted leading-relaxed">
        My technical work focuses on adaptive learning systems, multimodal AI architectures, 
        and the evaluation frameworks needed to build AI that actually helps people learn and grow. 
        I'm particularly interested in agentic collaboration—designing systems where humans and AI 
        work together as creative partners rather than master and servant.
      </p>

      <p class="font-body text-muted leading-relaxed">
        This site is where I explore ideas that span technical and philosophical territory. 
        Essays on learning system evaluation sit alongside reflections on meditation practice. 
        Deep dives into multimodal architectures coexist with thoughts on Sibelius and winter listening. 
        The connections between these domains are where the most interesting insights emerge.
      </p>

      <div class="border-l-3 border-primary pl-8 py-4 my-12">
        <p class="font-body text-muted leading-relaxed italic text-lg">
          I believe the most important work happens at boundaries—between disciplines, 
          between human and artificial intelligence, between the technical and the philosophical. 
          That's where this writing lives.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="font-body text-muted leading-relaxed">
        When I'm not building or writing, you'll find me deep in a classical music rabbit hole 
        (Rachmaninoff, Sibelius, and Mahler form my personal trinity), practicing meditation badly, 
        or being supervised by Luna and Mochi, my philosophical advisors who happen to be cats.
      </p>

      <p class="font-body text-muted leading-relaxed">
        I'm always interested in conversations about adaptive systems, learning design, 
        consciousness research, or the weird overlaps between technology and wisdom traditions. 
        The best ideas emerge in dialogue.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-gray-800">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-medium text-primary mb-4">This Site</h2>
        <p class="text-sm font-body text-muted leading-relaxed">
          Built with Astro, designed for reading, optimized for ideas worth your attention. 
          The source is available on GitHub for anyone curious about the implementation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
